1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,000
Το Plex ζήτησε 120€ για να συνεχίσετε να βλέπετε από τις συσκευές σας.
Το πλήρωσα εγώ το ποσό.

2
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:10,000
Αν χρησιμοποιείτε συχνά και μπορείτε,
 οποιαδήποτε συμβολή θα εκτιμηθεί.

3
00:01:59,820 --> 00:02:00,870
Frieren.

4
00:02:08,460 --> 00:02:10,580
The royal capital's in sight.

5
00:02:10,580 --> 00:02:13,460
The adventurers are making
their triumphant return.

6
00:02:13,460 --> 00:02:15,250
They must be celebrating in the city.

7
00:02:17,760 --> 00:02:20,340
We'll have to look for work once we're back.

8
00:02:20,840 --> 00:02:23,010
You're already thinking about that?

9
00:02:23,430 --> 00:02:25,010
It's important, after all.

10
00:02:25,010 --> 00:02:28,100
We've defeated the Demon King,
but it's not over.

11
00:02:28,930 --> 00:02:31,190
We have the whole rest
of our lives ahead of us.

12
00:02:31,900 --> 00:02:33,770
Work, huh?

13
00:02:33,770 --> 00:02:35,940
I'd like something where
I can drink on the job.

14
00:02:36,230 --> 00:02:37,530
Aren't you a priest?

15
00:02:40,200 --> 00:02:41,820
I suppose you're right.

16
00:02:43,950 --> 00:02:51,460
Frieren, the life ahead of you will surely
be much longer than we can imagine.

17
00:02:52,290 --> 00:02:53,630
Perhaps.

18
00:03:30,790 --> 00:03:32,500
Himmel the Hero,

19
00:03:32,870 --> 00:03:36,000
Eisen the Warrior, Heiter the Priest,

20
00:03:36,500 --> 00:03:38,750
and Frieren the Mage.

21
00:03:39,300 --> 00:03:42,930
Thank you for defeating the Demon King.

22
00:03:43,340 --> 00:03:48,010
Now our world will enter an age of peace.

23
00:04:02,990 --> 00:04:06,950
The king's going to erect
statues of us in the plaza.

24
00:04:07,370 --> 00:04:14,330
I'm not sure they'll be able to faithfully
recreate my handsome looks, though.

25
00:04:15,080 --> 00:04:16,920
How self-serving of him.

26
00:04:16,920 --> 00:04:20,500
He only gave us ten copper coins
when we left on our adventure.

27
00:04:22,130 --> 00:04:26,800
Now, now, Frieren.
Tonight, we drink for free.

28
00:04:26,800 --> 00:04:28,760
I'd say we're even, wouldn't you?

29
00:04:29,180 --> 00:04:30,470
You corrupt priest.

30
00:04:38,440 --> 00:04:40,230
It's over.

31
00:04:41,110 --> 00:04:42,230
Yeah.

32
00:04:42,990 --> 00:04:45,610
This is the end of our adventure.

33
00:04:46,450 --> 00:04:47,950
It's been ten years, huh?

34
00:04:48,620 --> 00:04:50,990
We've been through a lot.

35
00:04:52,040 --> 00:04:53,410
The day we departed...

36
00:04:54,040 --> 00:04:58,500
Himmel and Eisen were nearly executed
for speaking rudely to the king.

37
00:04:54,750 --> 00:04:55,830
Kill them.

38
00:04:56,580 --> 00:04:58,500
We'll give them a talking to.

39
00:04:57,330 --> 00:04:58,500
Shall we lick your boots?

40
00:04:58,790 --> 00:05:01,920
One misstep, and our adventure
would've ended there.

41
00:05:02,840 --> 00:05:06,550
Sometimes, Heiter was too
hungover to do anything.

42
00:05:10,850 --> 00:05:14,520
You're as pallid as an undead.
Are you all right?

43
00:05:14,520 --> 00:05:15,480
No.

44
00:05:15,480 --> 00:05:16,640
No, huh?

45
00:05:17,140 --> 00:05:19,400
It was a weekly occurrence.

46
00:05:19,650 --> 00:05:21,400
I, on the other hand, was exceptional.

47
00:05:21,650 --> 00:05:25,240
We thought about leaving you behind
when that mimic tried to eat you.

48
00:05:25,240 --> 00:05:28,410
Seriously? We told her it was a trap.

49
00:05:26,650 --> 00:05:30,120
It's dark and scary in here!

50
00:05:28,410 --> 00:05:30,120
Why don't we leave the elf behind?

51
00:05:34,750 --> 00:05:38,370
We have nothing but terrible memories.

52
00:05:39,710 --> 00:05:41,380
But I had fun.

53
00:05:41,880 --> 00:05:45,260
I'm glad I got to adventure with all of you.

54
00:05:46,050 --> 00:05:47,260
Likewise.

55
00:05:47,760 --> 00:05:50,010
It was a mere ten-year adventure.

56
00:05:50,260 --> 00:05:51,720
"A mere ten-year adventure"?

57
00:05:51,720 --> 00:05:54,140
But that's an entire decade
we spent adventuring together.

58
00:05:54,470 --> 00:05:58,100
Look at Heiter. He's turned into an old man.

59
00:05:58,100 --> 00:05:59,650
That's rude.

60
00:05:59,650 --> 00:06:01,190
He always looked like that.

61
00:06:01,190 --> 00:06:02,480
That's rude.

62
00:06:09,740 --> 00:06:11,240
It's nearly time.

63
00:06:19,290 --> 00:06:21,710
The Era Meteor Shower, was it?

64
00:06:22,330 --> 00:06:25,590
It happens once every fifty years.

65
00:06:26,630 --> 00:06:29,510
Perfect for marking the
start of an era of peace.

66
00:06:32,590 --> 00:06:34,260
They're beautiful.

67
00:06:34,260 --> 00:06:36,640
The view's not so good
from inside the city, though.

68
00:06:36,640 --> 00:06:39,770
I'm having a moment over here.
Don't spoil the mood.

69
00:06:41,850 --> 00:06:43,270
Next time, then.

70
00:06:45,070 --> 00:06:47,990
I know a place where you
can see them more clearly.

71
00:06:47,990 --> 00:06:49,530
I'll take you there in fifty years.

72
00:06:53,200 --> 00:06:54,410
What?

73
00:06:54,410 --> 00:06:56,740
It's nothing.

74
00:06:58,540 --> 00:07:01,750
You're right. Let's go see them together.

75
00:07:24,310 --> 00:07:26,020
Well, I should go.

76
00:07:26,570 --> 00:07:28,280
What are you going to do now?

77
00:07:28,820 --> 00:07:31,360
I'm going to continue collecting spells.

78
00:07:31,360 --> 00:07:34,870
I plan to travel around the central lands
for the next hundred years or so.

79
00:07:34,870 --> 00:07:37,240
I'll stop by once in a while.

80
00:07:42,330 --> 00:07:44,960
I can't understand what
being an elf must be like.

81
00:07:44,960 --> 00:07:47,630
Seriously, how long has she been around?

82
00:07:48,380 --> 00:07:53,630
To her, fifty or even a hundred years
might be a trifling thing.

83
00:08:44,060 --> 00:08:45,940
Shadow dragon horns?

84
00:08:46,230 --> 00:08:48,610
We don't have those here.

85
00:08:49,020 --> 00:08:52,940
Haven't seen a shadow dragon
in twenty or thirty years.

86
00:08:52,940 --> 00:08:56,950
I see. That's no good.
I need one for summoning.

87
00:08:59,530 --> 00:09:05,040
<i>Come to think of it, I think Himmel still has
the horn we got at the Demon King's castle.</i>

88
00:09:05,620 --> 00:09:08,960
It's exuding some kind of evil aura.

89
00:09:08,960 --> 00:09:10,920
It's not harmful to people, is it?

90
00:09:10,920 --> 00:09:12,050
I don't know.

91
00:09:12,050 --> 00:09:13,920
You don't know, huh?

92
00:09:14,630 --> 00:09:17,340
<i>It's nearly time for the
Era Meteor Shower again.</i>

93
00:09:17,340 --> 00:09:18,930
<i>I'll pick the horn up when I visit him.</i>

94
00:09:24,930 --> 00:09:28,350
<i>The city's changed quite a bit
since I was last here.</i>

95
00:09:42,740 --> 00:09:44,910
It should be around here.

96
00:09:45,620 --> 00:09:46,960
Frieren?

97
00:09:47,910 --> 00:09:48,750
Himmel...

98
00:09:55,630 --> 00:09:56,970
You're so old.

99
00:09:56,970 --> 00:09:58,380
Do you have to put it so bluntly?

100
00:10:00,800 --> 00:10:04,640
I'm still pretty handsome
at this age, though, aren't I?

101
00:10:06,060 --> 00:10:10,900
It's been fifty years.
You look the same as you ever did.

102
00:10:11,770 --> 00:10:15,110
I thought I'd never see you again.

103
00:10:17,490 --> 00:10:19,400
The Era Meteor Shower, huh?

104
00:10:19,700 --> 00:10:21,570
That brings back memories.

105
00:10:21,570 --> 00:10:24,740
About that thing we looted from
the Demon King's castle...

106
00:10:24,740 --> 00:10:26,790
You mean the shadow dragon horn?

107
00:10:27,120 --> 00:10:30,040
I've never forgotten about it.

108
00:10:30,500 --> 00:10:34,040
My cabinet's been exuding
an evil aura all this time.

109
00:10:34,500 --> 00:10:35,800
Sorry, I think.

110
00:10:36,380 --> 00:10:40,260
You could've stashed it
in a shed or something.

111
00:10:42,010 --> 00:10:43,930
I couldn't do that.

112
00:10:47,140 --> 00:10:51,850
You may not have thought much
of leaving it with me,

113
00:10:51,850 --> 00:10:57,440
but to me, it was a treasure
entrusted to me by a dear friend.

114
00:10:57,440 --> 00:11:01,200
I had to return it to you someday.

115
00:11:09,790 --> 00:11:12,750
It's not that big a deal.

116
00:11:32,600 --> 00:11:33,900
Himmel, are you ready yet?

117
00:11:34,600 --> 00:11:37,480
You're bald, anyway. There's no point
in fussing over your appearance.

118
00:11:38,360 --> 00:11:40,900
There are things we bald men
are particular about.

119
00:11:47,950 --> 00:11:51,540
Now, shall we go see the Era Meteor Shower?

120
00:11:59,710 --> 00:12:02,510
You've become rather dignified, Heiter.

121
00:12:02,510 --> 00:12:04,430
I'm a bishop of the holy city, after all.

122
00:12:04,720 --> 00:12:07,850
You haven't changed at all.

123
00:12:07,850 --> 00:12:09,680
Don't pat my head.

124
00:12:11,220 --> 00:12:13,520
Eisen, you haven't changed much.

125
00:12:14,140 --> 00:12:16,610
Is that how I seem to you?

126
00:12:16,610 --> 00:12:18,020
I would expect as much from a dwarf.

127
00:12:18,400 --> 00:12:21,490
So, where's this place where we can
see the meteor shower clearly?

128
00:12:22,400 --> 00:12:24,450
We're going there now?

129
00:12:24,450 --> 00:12:28,450
It's a bit early to see the
Era Meteor Shower, isn't it?

130
00:12:28,450 --> 00:12:32,540
Yeah. It's about a week's walk from here.

131
00:12:32,790 --> 00:12:35,040
It's that far away?

132
00:12:35,040 --> 00:12:36,630
Unbelievable.

133
00:12:36,630 --> 00:12:39,040
You should be kinder to the elderly.

134
00:12:42,340 --> 00:12:43,880
This brings back memories.

135
00:12:44,260 --> 00:12:48,050
Traveling together like this makes me
feel like we've returned to those days.

136
00:12:52,470 --> 00:12:55,060
We journeyed to all sorts of places.

137
00:12:56,020 --> 00:13:01,070
Everything seemed so brilliant and new.

138
00:13:25,880 --> 00:13:30,930
And you were always there
in those beautiful memories.

139
00:13:34,100 --> 00:13:39,770
I'd been looking forward to the day
when we'd all be together again.

140
00:13:40,480 --> 00:13:42,400
Thank you, Frieren.

141
00:13:43,320 --> 00:13:48,700
Because of you, I had this delightful
adventure at the very end.

142
00:14:12,720 --> 00:14:14,350
They're beautiful.

143
00:14:41,460 --> 00:14:44,880
I think Himmel was happy.

144
00:14:46,340 --> 00:14:47,840
You think so?

145
00:14:54,800 --> 00:14:57,930
She was one of Mr. Himmel's companions?

146
00:14:58,270 --> 00:15:00,440
I haven't seen her look sad once today.

147
00:15:00,690 --> 00:15:02,650
How heartless.

148
00:15:03,650 --> 00:15:07,320
Now, now! We're not wearing
sad expressions, either.

149
00:15:07,320 --> 00:15:08,860
Show some respect, Bishop!

150
00:15:08,860 --> 00:15:10,070
You're heartless!

151
00:15:11,700 --> 00:15:13,110
You wound me.

152
00:15:37,060 --> 00:15:41,390
It's not like I knew anything about him.

153
00:15:53,490 --> 00:15:57,370
We only traveled together
for a mere ten years.

154
00:16:04,460 --> 00:16:08,840
I knew human lives were short, but...

155
00:16:10,090 --> 00:16:14,880
Why didn't I try to get to know him better?

156
00:16:23,980 --> 00:16:26,190
Don't pat my head.

157
00:16:34,820 --> 00:16:37,990
I should return to the holy city.

158
00:16:41,080 --> 00:16:43,750
Let me get a good look at your faces.

159
00:16:44,330 --> 00:16:46,620
This will probably be
the last time I see you.

160
00:16:47,040 --> 00:16:48,380
Are you unwell?

161
00:16:48,750 --> 00:16:51,130
My years of drinking have caught up to me.

162
00:16:51,460 --> 00:16:52,880
It's divine punishment.

163
00:16:54,380 --> 00:16:59,010
If you're ever in the holy city,
offer a drink at my grave.

164
00:17:00,890 --> 00:17:03,560
Heiter, you're not afraid of dying?

165
00:17:05,690 --> 00:17:09,480
We're the party of adventurers
that saved the world.

166
00:17:09,480 --> 00:17:13,230
We'll surely be living the good life
in Heaven after death.

167
00:17:13,860 --> 00:17:17,950
That's the whole reason
I fought alongside you.

168
00:17:17,950 --> 00:17:19,530
You corrupt priest.

169
00:17:21,790 --> 00:17:23,500
If you'll excuse me.

170
00:17:31,710 --> 00:17:34,710
I should get going, too.

171
00:17:35,510 --> 00:17:37,720
You're off to collect more spells?

172
00:17:37,720 --> 00:17:39,550
There's that, too,

173
00:17:40,430 --> 00:17:43,430
but I want to learn more about humans.

174
00:17:45,560 --> 00:17:46,520
I see.

175
00:17:47,520 --> 00:17:49,940
So I wanted to ask you something.

176
00:17:49,940 --> 00:17:55,030
Seeing as how I'm a mage, having a powerful
warrior to defend me would be a huge help.

177
00:17:55,030 --> 00:17:56,740
Give me a break.

178
00:17:57,070 --> 00:17:59,990
I'm too old to swing an axe now.

179
00:18:03,280 --> 00:18:05,830
Don't make that face, Frieren.

180
00:18:06,200 --> 00:18:11,130
Surprisingly, life slows down
once you've lost your vigor.

181
00:18:12,960 --> 00:18:13,880
I see.

182
00:18:14,670 --> 00:18:16,880
I'll see you later, Eisen.

183
00:18:17,260 --> 00:18:18,880
Yeah. See you later.

184
00:19:00,430 --> 00:19:02,430
That's the tree I saw earlier.

185
00:19:02,430 --> 00:19:04,300
I always get lost in these woods.

186
00:19:05,100 --> 00:19:06,600
Where am I?

187
00:19:10,980 --> 00:19:13,060
Are you looking for something?

188
00:19:18,360 --> 00:19:20,070
Is something the matter?

189
00:19:20,950 --> 00:19:24,950
I'm looking for the home
of a man named Heiter.

190
00:19:24,950 --> 00:19:27,620
Then you're a visitor.

191
00:19:30,580 --> 00:19:33,210
You're still alive, you corrupt priest?

192
00:19:34,630 --> 00:19:38,250
Turns out it's harder than I thought
to make a stylish exit.

193
00:19:38,630 --> 00:19:41,010
I brought some liquor to offer at your grave.

194
00:19:41,380 --> 00:19:42,630
Would you like a drink?

195
00:19:42,630 --> 00:19:44,970
I gave up drinking.

196
00:19:44,970 --> 00:19:45,800
I see.

197
00:19:46,470 --> 00:19:51,390
I doubt the Goddess will forgive you
even if you clean up your act now.

198
00:19:58,480 --> 00:20:00,490
Thank you.

199
00:20:05,530 --> 00:20:06,620
Who is she?

200
00:20:06,910 --> 00:20:08,490
Her name is Fern.

201
00:20:08,490 --> 00:20:11,830
She's a war orphan from the southern lands.

202
00:20:13,250 --> 00:20:18,420
It's not like you to
volunteer to help people.

203
00:20:18,420 --> 00:20:20,090
You're not Himmel, after all.

204
00:20:22,840 --> 00:20:25,930
Frieren, why did you come to visit me?

205
00:20:25,930 --> 00:20:28,100
I was in the holy city
picking up some things.

206
00:20:28,600 --> 00:20:32,430
I've been trying to get to know the people
I meet on my travels as much as possible.

207
00:20:33,430 --> 00:20:38,440
And I owe you a lot, so I came to
repay my debts before you died.

208
00:20:41,940 --> 00:20:44,200
In that case, I have a request.

209
00:20:45,320 --> 00:20:47,280
Will you take on an apprentice?

210
00:20:49,120 --> 00:20:53,040
Fern has potential as a mage.

211
00:20:53,040 --> 00:20:56,170
Will you take her with you on your travels?

212
00:20:59,040 --> 00:21:02,170
I'm sorry, Heiter.
That's the one thing I can't do.

213
00:21:02,460 --> 00:21:04,130
She'd only get in my way.

214
00:21:05,430 --> 00:21:09,300
You know how often
apprentice mages die in battle.

215
00:21:10,010 --> 00:21:13,680
I'm not sending a child my friend
asked me to look after to her death.

216
00:21:16,810 --> 00:21:20,610
I see. Then I have another request.

217
00:21:26,200 --> 00:21:29,660
This was unearthed from
the tomb of Ewig the Sage.

218
00:21:30,280 --> 00:21:37,460
This grimoire is said to contain lost
spells of resurrection and immortality.

219
00:21:37,790 --> 00:21:41,090
I find it hard to believe
such magic really exists.

220
00:21:41,380 --> 00:21:45,090
That's part of why I'd like you to decipher it.

221
00:21:45,340 --> 00:21:46,590
Can you do that?

222
00:21:47,180 --> 00:21:49,390
It's written in code using pictures.

223
00:21:49,390 --> 00:21:52,180
The people of this era
really liked this kind of thing.

224
00:21:52,600 --> 00:21:54,970
I could do it, given five or six years.

225
00:21:55,640 --> 00:21:57,190
I see.

226
00:21:57,730 --> 00:22:00,770
But why do you want this deciphered?

227
00:22:00,770 --> 00:22:03,440
I thought you weren't afraid of dying.

228
00:22:03,440 --> 00:22:05,570
I have two reasons.

229
00:22:06,030 --> 00:22:10,570
The first is that I when I said that,
I was just putting on a brave face for you.

230
00:22:10,820 --> 00:22:14,950
The second is that I'm now more
afraid of dying than I was before.

231
00:22:15,830 --> 00:22:24,130
Even if I can't achieve immortality,
I'd like a bit more time.

232
00:22:28,170 --> 00:22:32,390
Besides, the holy texts tell us
to live healthy lives.

233
00:22:32,390 --> 00:22:35,600
A long life is the ultimate
expression of that, Frieren.

234
00:22:35,600 --> 00:22:37,270
You corrupt priest.

235
00:22:39,440 --> 00:22:46,360
Also, in your spare time,
will you teach Fern magic?

236
00:22:46,730 --> 00:22:50,990
As a priest, I don't have that knowledge.

237
00:22:51,740 --> 00:22:54,080
I could do that.

238
00:23:01,750 --> 00:23:02,920
There you are.

239
00:23:04,340 --> 00:23:06,670
I've been looking everywhere for you.

240
00:23:06,670 --> 00:23:08,760
Do you always train in the woods?

241
00:23:09,130 --> 00:23:13,340
Was finding me difficult even for you?

242
00:23:13,930 --> 00:23:18,140
Mr. Heiter often tells me
I'm practically invisible.

243
00:23:19,810 --> 00:23:22,310
It's a very good thing, isn't it?

244
00:23:23,650 --> 00:23:25,020
It is.

245
00:23:27,860 --> 00:23:32,030
<i>It's true. I can barely detect her mana.</i>

246
00:23:32,490 --> 00:23:34,990
<i>Her control over her mana is exceptional.</i>

247
00:23:35,830 --> 00:23:39,290
<i>How much has she studied at such a young age?</i>

248
00:23:39,700 --> 00:23:45,790
Mr. Heiter said when I can blast a hole
in that rock, I'll be a proper mage.

249
00:23:46,210 --> 00:23:49,710
Oh? Heiter knows what he's
talking about. That's—

250
00:23:55,890 --> 00:23:59,720
As you just saw, my magic
dissipates and doesn't reach it.

251
00:24:00,480 --> 00:24:01,730
I see.

252
00:24:02,390 --> 00:24:05,270
What should I do to train?

253
00:24:05,610 --> 00:24:08,480
Can I ask you something first?

254
00:24:09,480 --> 00:24:10,990
Do you like magic?

255
00:24:11,780 --> 00:24:13,490
Somewhat.

256
00:24:16,070 --> 00:24:17,950
Just like me, then.

257
00:25:50,250 --> 00:25:53,210
Is Fern's training coming along smoothly?

258
00:25:50,250 --> 00:25:53,210
Are you trying to put on
a brave face again, Heiter?

259
00:25:51,290 --> 00:25:53,210
It saddens me to see him treated like this.

260
00:25:53,210 --> 00:25:55,170
But they're worth looking for.

261
00:25:53,210 --> 00:25:55,170
Magic sure is amazing, isn't it?

262
00:25:53,210 --> 00:25:55,170
You keep collecting the strangest spells.

263
00:25:55,170 --> 00:25:56,760
It'd be a waste for you to die.

264
00:25:55,170 --> 00:25:57,800
Someday, I'd like to show them to you.

265
00:25:57,800 --> 00:25:59,970
It didn't have to be magic...
